+This is a newly authored, fixture-local record cluster. Its Japanese mythology comparison is limited to three clauses in Basil Hall Chamberlain's 1882 translation of *The Kojiki*; it is not a retelling, an in-world source, or a claim about all Japanese traditions or contemporary Shinto practice. The translated source excerpt remains separate from the fictional `sources.json` record.
+
+The local fiction concerns Urell, Dovren, and Veshra comparing marks on a paper record. All fictional names, source IDs, place and item names, relation, event IDs, and local ticks are original fixture labels. No named person, deity, place, or object in the external passage becomes an in-world referent.
+
