+The first command checks JSON shape and local IDs. The second checks the map inventory, R9 mode declarations, and fixed-string anchors in their stated spans. Neither establishes historical truth, translation fidelity, permission, or canon.
+
+## Three citation questions
+
+`inspiration-note.md` keeps attribution, rights for the delivered translation/transcription, and AI-training permission as three independent questions. The translation is not used as source support for fictional JSON. Every fictional fact cites the newly authored `archive-slip` text in `verbatim` mode; the external rows in the map are editorial clause references only.
+
